# Ship-gate workflow

Start and finish product work from a Cursor agent request. Do not auto-merge, auto-deploy to hosting, or create a GitHub Release without an explicit user choice at each gate.

EASM is **self-hosted**: shelters download or clone the app and install on their own web hosting. Agents must **never** invent Cloudron/`workflow_dispatch` deploy steps, push code to customer servers, or assume a live production URL.

## Pre-commit verification (required)

Before the **commit gate**, run and record results (source `scripts/local/use-laragon.ps1` on Windows):

1. **Tests** — `composer test` (full suite). Must exit 0.
2. **Lint** — `composer lint` once. Must exit 0. If it fails: at most one `composer format`, then re-run lint once. Do not loop or run Pint mid-work.
3. **UI smoke** (when the slice touched HTTP/views/routes) — Laragon Apache + MySQL up; `GET http://easm.test/health` returns ok (or same URL with `Host: easm.test` if DNS is not set); quick browser smoke of the changed path.

If any step fails: report failures, fix or stop. **Do not** present commit / commit+PR options. WIP commits only when the user explicitly asks to save broken work.

No secrets (`.env`, credentials) staged.

## Gates

At each gate, end the turn with a numbered list of next best actions and **one recommended reply**. Wait for the user before continuing.

### Commit gate (after verification passes)

Recommended usually: commit and open/update the PR when the slice is reviewable.

1. Commit now
2. Commit and open/update PR
3. Keep working uncommitted

Never commit silently — this gate *is* the ask.

### After PR CI is green

Recommended usually: merge when checks are OK.

1. Merge the PR
2. Fix remaining review / CI issues
3. Leave PR open / stop

Never merge unless the user already ordered merge or picks option 1.

### After merge is verified on `main`

There is **no deploy gate**. Installs stay download + Composer + `/install` (see README).

Recommended: skip release unless the user already asked to cut one.

1. Create GitHub Release now
2. Skip release / stop

Never create the release silently. Confirm tag/version with the user when unclear (`APP_VERSION` / `config('app.version')` today; no root `VERSION` / `releases.json` yet).

## Completion

Only after merge is verified, and after any chosen GitHub Release succeeds, give the completion confirmation (PR URL/number, merge SHA, target branch, release URL if created, linked issue closed/updated). Offer to archive the agent; do not archive silently.
